{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,55p' src/dev/affected_test.clj && sed -n '235,280p' src/dev/affected_test.clj && tail -25 src/dev/affected_test.clj\"","aggregated_output":"(ns affected-test\n  \"Tests of the pure functions of src/dev/affected.clj.\n\n   Babashka only (affected.clj reads ns forms with edamame). It lives\n   under src/dev, not test/, so the JVM lane's runner never loads it.\n\n   Run with babashka:\n     bb -cp src/dev -m affected-test\"\n  (:require\n    [affected :as a]\n    [clojure.string :as str]\n    [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing run-tests]]))\n\n\n(deftest classify-sorts-changed-paths\n  (testing \"ignored trees and markdown\"\n    (doseq [p [\"docs/design/x.md\" \"collab/1-a.prompt.md\" \"build/x.jar\"\n               \"target/node-tests.js\" \"node_modules/a/index.js\"\n               \"README.md\" \"src/cljc/yin/README.md\"]]\n      (is (= :ignored (a/classify p)) p)))\n  (testing \"a markdown fixture under test/resources is a resource\"\n    (is (= :resource (a/classify \"test/resources/dao/x/errata.md\"))))\n  (testing \"wide changes\"\n    (doseq [p [\"deps.edn\" \"bb.edn\" \"shadow-cljs.edn\" \"tests.edn\"\n               \".clj-kondo/config.edn\" \"antlr/python3/manifest.edn\"\n               \"src/dev/cljd_agg.clj\" \"package.json\" \"pubspec.yaml\"\n               \"mise.toml\" \".cljstyle\"]]\n      (is (= :wide (a/classify p)) p)))\n  (testing \"code under src/ and test/\"\n    (doseq [p [\"src/cljc/a/b.cljc\" \"src/clj/a/b.clj\" \"src/cljs/a/b.cljs\"\n               \"src/cljd/a/b.cljd\" \"test/a/b_test.cljc\"]]\n      (is (= :code (a/classify p)) p)))\n  (testing \"generated Dart output is ignored\"\n    (is (= :ignored (a/classify \"test/cljd-out/a/b_test.dart\"))))\n  (testing \"anything else is a resource\"\n    (is (= :resource (a/classify \"test/resources/yin/x-v1.txt\")))\n    (is (= :resource (a/classify \"src/shaders/a.frag\")))))\n\n\n(deftest form-deps-reads-every-libspec-shape\n  (let [form '(ns foo.bar\n                (:refer-clojure :exclude [map])\n                (:require\n                  a.plain\n                  [b.vec]\n                  [c.as :as c]\n                  [d.refer :refer [x y]]\n                  [e.prefix f g.h [i :as i] [j :refer [z]]]\n                  [\"npm-lib\" :as npm]\n                  :reload)\n                (:use [k.use :only [w]] l.use)\n                (:require-macros [m.macros :refer [mac]])\n                (:import (java.util UUID)))]\n    (is (= 'foo.bar (a/ns-name-of form)))\n    (is (= '#{a.plain b.vec c.as d.refer e.prefix.f e.prefix.g.h\n         (a/parse-summary :clj (str \"Ran 12 tests containing 40 assertions.\\n\"\n                                    \"2 failures, 1 errors.\\n\"))))\n  (is (= {:tests 7 :failures 0}\n         (a/parse-summary :cljs (str \"Ran 7 tests containing 9 assertions.\\n\"\n                                     \"0 failures, 0 errors.\\n\"))))\n  (is (= {:tests 33 :failures 2}\n         (a/parse-summary :cljd (str \"00:01 +3: a\\n00:09 +31 ~1 -2: \"\n                                     \"Some tests failed.\\n\"))))\n  (is (= {:tests 5 :failures 0}\n         (a/parse-summary :cljd \"00:03 +5: All tests passed!\\n\")))\n  (is (= {:tests nil :failures nil} (a/parse-summary :clj \"boom\"))))\n\n\n(deftest prerequisites-follow-the-forward-closure\n  (let [idx [(entry \"src/clj/r/spawn.clj\"\n                    \"(ns r.spawn)\\n(def js \\\"target/yin-repl.js\\\")\")\n             (entry \"src/clj/r/parse.clj\"\n                    \"(ns r.parse (:import (x Python3Parser)))\")\n             (entry \"test/r/spawn_test.clj\"\n                    \"(ns r.spawn-test (:require [r.spawn]))\")\n             (entry \"test/r/parse_test.clj\"\n                    \"(ns r.parse-test (:require [r.parse]))\")\n             (entry \"test/r/peer_test.cljc\"\n                    \"(ns r.peer-test)\\n(def e \\\"build/yin-repl-peer\\\")\")\n             (entry \"test/r/plain_test.cljc\" \"(ns r.plain-test)\")]]\n    (is (= #{:build:yin-repl-node}\n           (a/prerequisites idx {:clj '[r.spawn-test]})))\n    (is (= #{:gen:python-antlr}\n           (a/prerequisites idx {:clj '[r.parse-test]})))\n    (is (= #{} (a/prerequisites idx {:cljs '[r.parse-test]}))\n        \"the ANTLR classes are a JVM-lane need only\")\n    (is (= #{:build:yin-repl-peer}\n           (a/prerequisites idx {:cljd '[r.peer-test]})))\n    (is (= #{} (a/prerequisites idx {:clj '[r.plain-test]\n                                     :cljs '[r.plain-test]})))))\n\n\n(deftest serialized-pairs-detects-a-jvm-cljd-build\n  (let [idx [(entry \"test/r/build_test.clj\"\n                    (str \"(ns r.build-test)\\n(def c [\\\"clojure\\\"\"\n                         \" \\\"-M:clojuredart:cljd\\\" \\\"compile\\\"])\"))\n             (entry \"test/r/plain_test.cljc\" \"(ns r.plain-test)\")]]\n    (is (= #{[:clj :cljd]}\n           (a/serialized-pairs idx {:clj '[r.build-test]\n                                    :cljd '[r.plain-test]})))\n    (is (= #{} (a/serialized-pairs idx {:clj '[r.build-test]})))\n      (doseq [t test-nses]\n        (let [s (a/match-subsystem sub-cfg t)]\n          (is (some? s) (str \"test namespace has no subsystem: \" t)))))\n    (testing \"every prefix matches at least one namespace in the codebase\"\n      (let [matches-prefix? (fn [p ns-str]\n                              (or (= ns-str p)\n                                  (str/starts-with? ns-str (str p \".\"))\n                                  (str/starts-with? ns-str (str p \"-\"))))]\n        (doseq [s (:subsystems sub-cfg)\n                p (:prefixes s)]\n          (is (seq (filter #(matches-prefix? p (str %)) all-nses))\n              (str \"prefix matches no namespace: \" p)))))\n    (testing \"selection by subsystem name returns the expected set\"\n      (let [ucf-tests (a/select-subsystems index sub-cfg [\"yin.vm.ucf\"])]\n        (is (= 40 (count ucf-tests)))\n        (is (contains? ucf-tests 'yin.vm.ucf.compose-test))))\n    (testing \"unknown subsystem throws\"\n      (is (thrown? clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo\n            (a/select-subsystems index sub-cfg [\"unknown.subsystem\"]))))))\n\n\n(defn -main\n  [& _]\n  (let [{:keys [fail error]} (run-tests 'affected-test)]\n    (System/exit (if (zero? (+ fail error)) 0 1))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '475,545p' docs/agents/build-n-test.md && rg -n 'test:clj|gen:antlr' bb.edn | head -35 && command -v bb && command -v clj && command -v clj-kondo && git remote -v\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '475,545p' docs/agents/build-n-test.md && rg -n 'test:clj|gen:antlr' bb.edn | head -35 && command -v bb && command -v clj && command -v clj-kondo && git remote -v\"","aggregated_output":"|---|---|---|\n| `shiva.stigmergy.systems` | 24 / 62 GB | Server snapshot: java 21, clojure 1.12.4.1602, node 25.6.1, babashka, cljstyle, zprint, flutter 3.47.1. The repo's `mise.toml` selects Flutter `latest` on beta, not a fixed version. Activate the repo toolchain before running any lane. |\n| `jupiter.stigmergy.systems` | 48 / 62 GB | Server snapshot (rechecked 2026-10-29): java 21, clojure 1.12.4.1602, node 25.6.1, babashka, cljstyle, zprint, flutter 3.47.8 (the stale hand-symlinked 3.41.9 was replaced via `mise install flutter@3.47.8` after it failed to compile `dart:ui`-using cljd namespaces; if the Dart lane dies in the cljd compile, check `mise ls flutter` first). Tri-host quick tier verified green on 2026-10-29 (see Measured times). |\n\n**Never test in `~/workspace/datomworld` on either host.** It is a working copy\nthat is behind origin (shiva: 45 commits behind on 2026-10-11) and belongs to its\nowner. Use a scratch clone under `~/ci/` and leave the working copy alone.\n\n### Get the code there: push to origin, never rsync\n\nRsyncing a worktree over the WAN ran at about 150 KB/s (576 MB of tracked files\nwould take about an hour), and an unanchored `--exclude build` also dropped source\ndirectories named `build`, `out` and `target`. Both hosts reach GitHub, so push the\nbranch from the laptop (a feature branch, never master), make one scratch clone on\nthe host from its existing checkout (a local clone takes seconds), and fetch:\n\n```sh\n# once per host: a separate scratch clone, not the working copy\nssh shiva.stigmergy.systems 'set -e; mkdir -p ~/ci; cd ~/workspace/datomworld;\n  URL=$(git remote get-url origin);\n  git clone -q --no-checkout ~/workspace/datomworld ~/ci/datomworld-<name>;\n  cd ~/ci/datomworld-<name>; git remote set-url origin \"$URL\";\n  git fetch -q origin; git checkout -q --detach origin/<branch>'\n```\n\nTo test another branch later, fetch and check it out in the scratch clone with\n`git fetch origin` then `git checkout --detach origin/<branch>`. A branch that\nwas never pushed cannot be tested remotely.\n\n### Activate the toolchain in the right order\n\nA non-interactive `ssh host cmd` does not load the shell profile, so `mise` and its\ntools are not on PATH. In a script, do this in exactly this order, after the `cd`\ninto the clone:\n\n```sh\nexport PATH=\"$HOME/.local/bin:/snap/bin:$PATH\"   # mise: ~/.local/bin on shiva, /snap/bin on jupiter\ncd ~/ci/datomworld-<name>\nmise trust >/dev/null 2>&1                       # trust is per path; a fresh clone is untrusted\nmise install                                    # install versions selected by this checkout's mise.toml\neval \"$(mise env -s bash)\"                       # puts the repo-selected tools on PATH\nmise current flutter                            # verify the selected Flutter version\n```\n\nActivating mise before the `cd` and `mise trust` leaves the repo-selected tools\n(flutter in particular) off PATH: the Dart lane then dies in seconds with \"Can't\nfind flutter on PATH\", and so does `bb build:yin-repl-peer`.\n\n### Which lanes may overlap (reconciling the one-lane-set rule)\n\n\"One lane set at a time\" and \"one Dart lane at a time\" are per-machine rules about\nCPU: they exist because a laptop has 8 cores. They are not a rule about repos.\n`test.subsystems.md` section 5 item 6 says the same (\"on one machine where\navoidable\"). The laptop additionally never runs the slow tier or the nightly\ndriver (see the sharded-lane section) — a full slow tier there reached a load\naverage over 100 on 2026-11-01; the remote hosts own that tier. On shiva (24 cores) and jupiter (48) the cores are not the limit, so\nlanes may overlap, with these limits:\n\n- **JVM and Dart lanes must not share one clone.** `src/dev/affected.clj`\n  (`serialized-pairs`, the `[:clj :cljd]` pair) serializes them whenever a JVM test\n  runs the cljd compiler, and some do (`yin.repl.build-test`,\n  `yin.vm.linker.cross-host-transfer-test`, `dao.stream.ws-project-cross-jvm-test`);\n  the compiler writes the clone's `lib/cljd-out` and `build/`. A second scratch clone\n  gives the Dart lane its own copies, so the two lanes then overlap safely. This is\n  by the design's own reasoning (\"each worktree owns its own `cljd-out`\"), not yet\n  verified by a measured run.\n- **JVM and Node may share a clone.** Node writes `target/` and `.shadow-cljs/`; the\n  JVM lane only reads `target/yin-repl.js`.\n- **One Dart lane per host at a time**, even across clones: the lane shards up to\n  `min(8, cores)` Flutter processes and shares the host's Flutter cache.\n- **Different branches in different clones** are independent, so two branches may\n2: {gen:antlr\n233:   ;; The Node lanes (test:cljs and its variants) depend on this task, so the\n235:   :depends [deps:npm gen:antlr]\n244:   :depends [gen:antlr]\n251:   ;; and Node lanes, so `bb test` builds it first; a bare `bb test:clj` or\n252:   ;; `bb test:cljs` without it skips those tests with a printed notice\n263:   :depends [deps:npm gen:antlr]\n267:  test:clj {:doc \"JVM tests, fast: skips ^:slow ones; the DHT process test needs the Node REPL build\"\n268:            :depends [build:yin-repl-node gen:antlr]\n275:  test:cljs {:doc \"Node tests, fast: dao.test-slow guarded bodies print SKIP; needs the Node REPL build\"\n279:  test:cljd {:doc \"Dart tests, fast: aggregated shards via src/dev/cljd_agg.clj; guarded bodies print SKIP\"\n285:                :depends [build:yin-repl-node gen:antlr]\n301:                 :depends [build:yin-repl-node gen:antlr]\n327:        :depends [build:yin-repl-peer build:yin-repl-node test:clj test:cljs test:cljd]}\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"The existing Babashka test already covers this heuristic, but its ANTLR expectation is stale: it names the retired task and asserts that CLJS never needs it. I’ll update that focused test to cover each lane and retain the unrelated-selection checks. The standalone `bb test:clj` task declares `gen:antlr` directly, so this change only affects the selection-based runners."}}
